# SimpleOS production status ledger — canonical owner + maturity per subsystem.
# Master plan: doc/01_research/domain/simpleos_production_host_master_plan.md §22 Phase 0.
# Guarded by test/01_unit/os/arch/duplicate_owner_spec.spl (ledger/code parity).
# maturity: production | partial | model | evidence-only | host-proxy | stub | duplicate
# Progress notes reflect landed+pushed convergence tranches (2026-07-27):
#   Stage S/P/INT, T2 (container/DeviceGrant/flock), T3-T4 (Podman-MDSOC+ mgr+OCI),
#   FV/FV2 (Lean proofs), SVC (service_v1), UPD (TUF), SQ (SQLite-VFS contract).

production_status:
  abi_contract:
    owner: os.kernel.abi.abi_v1
    lane: A00
    maturity: partial
    note: ABI v1 frozen by reference (Stage S); duplicate-owner guard green
  kernel_types:
    owner: os.kernel.types
    lane: A00
    maturity: production
  ipc:
    owner: os.kernel.ipc
    lane: A01
    maturity: partial
    note: single-use capability guard landed + Lean-proven (SingleUse); l4_fast_ipc marked honest model; reply object landed as MODEL only (reply_object.spl — one-shot reply cap reusing SingleUseLedger, call/notify distinction, caller-death invalidation, atomic deny-wins handle transfer via spawn_with_cspace_tracked; spec reply_object_spec.spl); NOT wired to syscall_ipc and NOT on any boot path; full endpoint/reply/notification fastpath + two-process QEMU call/reply evidence still OUTSTANDING (gate in .spipe/ipc_reply_object/state.md)
  capability_spawn:
    owner: os.kernel.ipc.cspace_spawn
    lane: A02
    maturity: model
    note: root-only ambient-spawn guard wired (3/3 sites); boot seal GATED OFF pending SpawnSpec migration + QEMU boot evidence; live child CSpace injection still pending; P8xP2 profile meet-point landed (spawn_effective_rights_with_profile, contract spec 16 examples 0 failures)
  loader:
    owner: os.kernel.loader
    lane: A02
    maturity: partial
    note: spawn_authority guard + effective-rights helpers landed; descriptor-based exec pending
  memory:
    owner: os.kernel.memory
    lane: A02
    maturity: partial
  vfs:
    owner: os.kernel.fs
    lane: A03
    maturity: partial
    note: VfsHandleTable handle->mount routing landed (8 mounts[0] bypasses removed in services/vfs + LLM dispatch); src/lib fs_driver + 4 FAT32 copies still coexist — full collapse multi-increment; FAT32 copies 4->3, deleted src/lib/nogc_sync_mut/fs_driver/fat32_{core,dir_ops,hardening,parsers,stub,test_device}.spl (3165 lines, shadowed dead code: std.fs_driver.* resolves nogc_async_mut first, zero explicit importers; proven by async-only-symbol probe + failing sync-path control). FAT32B increment: sync fs_driver tier collapsed to shims — deleted ramfs/mount_table/direct_io/extension/driver_adapter/instance/ops (2477 lines, same shadowing, 15-vs-15 lockstep commit history, zero explicit importers) + orphaned fat32_cache.spl and its 2 spec copies (1017 lines; VFS2 delete-condition resolved: async fat32_core has 0 Dict refs / 77 flat-cache-field refs, never adopted it, and doc/09_report/nogc_eviction_leak_audit_2026-07-25.md confirms a leak in its 4 classes). −3494 net; 25 stale @cover paths repointed to async + 1 VFS2 dangling read_file guard repaired; all spec block counts byte-identical to baseline, Stage-S duplicate_owner guard 7 ✓/0 ✗, resolve probe PASS on JIT and interpreter. FAT32C increment: retired legacy driver deleted — src/os/services/fat32/{fat32,fat32_write,fat32_filesystem_ops,fat32_write_helpers}.spl (2122 lines) plus its 2 orphaned fat32_spec.spl copies (106 lines); island re-verified independently (zero src/ importers, imported only by each other, shared_fat32_driver delegates to std.fs_driver.fat32_core, no boot path / image builder / .shs reference). vfs_pure_fat_production_guard_spec.spl guard block was NOT removed but STRENGTHENED from non-use to absence: _assert_legacy_fat_implementation_files_deleted() asserts the 4 paths never reappear under src/os, and the tree walk lost its 4-file exemption so it now covers all of src/os; negative control confirmed the new assertion fails when the files are present (JIT + interpreter). −2232 net (git diff --stat: 22 insertions / 2254 deletions). All 15 vfs/arch/fs_driver spec block counts byte-identical to baseline; Stage-S duplicate_owner guard 7 ✓/0 ✗ on JIT and interpreter. FAT32 copies 3->2 — remaining: src/os/kernel/fs/fat32.spl (813, blocked on a target_presets.spl allowed_families decision, boot-path change needing QEMU+board validation); plan in .spipe/fs_stack_collapse/state.md §6 and .spipe/fat32_island_deletion/state.md
  drivers:
    owner: os.drivers
    lane: A04
    maturity: partial
    note: DeviceGrant runtime ABI + 10-step crash-revocation ordering landed + Lean-proven (no-DMA-without-IOMMU); wiring into real driver bind/crash path pending
  posix:
    owner: os.posix
    lane: A05
    maturity: partial
    note: writable shared mmap now has a kernel MODEL (vmm_shared.spl shared page-cache objects + rights attenuation + msync/last-unmap write-back; spec 7 blocks/35 examples/0 failures on JIT and interpreter); physical-frame path unproven (needs OVMF QEMU two-task gate), libc mmap still fails closed EOPNOTSUPP, syscall/VFS wiring not landed, SQLite WAL still blocked; no pthreads
  tty:
    owner: os.kernel tty paths
    lane: A06
    maturity: partial
    note: tty_write now delivers bytes to a drainable output buffer; PTY master/slave round-trip pending
  ssh:
    owner: os simple-native sshd
    lane: A06
    maturity: model
    note: x86_64-only FS-exec arms; OpenSSH port is the production path (multi-week, blocked)
  containers:
    owner: os container contract
    lane: A07
    maturity: partial
    note: kernel ContainerNamespaceView rootless deny-by-default enforcement + Lean-proven isolation; Podman-on-MDSOC+ manager (sys_create/pod_wire/start/stop) + OCI edge adapter landed; live lookup-site wiring + boot evidence pending
  web_server:
    owner: os.http
    lane: A09
    maturity: partial
    note: native raw benchmark fast; routed server interpreter-bound
  database:
    owner: simple db embedded (SDN store)
    lane: A09
    maturity: partial
    note: SQLite sqlite3_vfs contract landed (rollback-journal supported, WAL honestly gated on absent shared mmap); actual SQLite amalgamation build is multi-session (C toolchain blocked); server tier absent
  config:
    owner: std.config (to extract from IDE config)
    lane: A10
    maturity: partial
    note: std.config core extracted to src/lib/common/config_core (schema+layers, mandatory-as-ceiling); IDE call-site swap pending; second non-IDE consumer = std.test_runner.test_config (TestConfig schema + workspace/session/mandatory layers, hand-rolled merge deleted)
  browser:
    owner: browser tree
    lane: A10
    maturity: model
    note: production-blocking isolation/origin/lifecycle gaps (renderer/network/GPU split multi-session)
  llm_profiles:
    owner: os security llm profile registry
    lane: A07
    maturity: partial
    note: profile registry (deny-wins intersection, 6 built-ins) + spawn effective-rights adapter landed + Lean-proven attenuation; live spawn-syscall wiring pending; P8xP2 meet-point landed (adapter routes through spawn_authority.spawn_effective_rights_with_profile)
  service_manifest:
    owner: os.services.service_manifest
    lane: A06
    maturity: partial
    note: typed service_v1 lifecycle/health/watchdog/restart-limit + §21 restart-drops-stale-grants invariant; 2 real services declaring — container_manager (restart drops manifest grants + brokered-out container pouches/views), tty_service (restart drops device grants + per-TTY pending-signal targeting); proven by test/01_unit/os/services/service_manifest_integration_spec.spl (9 blocks, 16 examples, 0 failures)
  update_tuf:
    owner: os.services.update.tuf_metadata
    lane: A07
    maturity: model
    note: TUF 4-role verifier (rollback/freeze/threshold/snapshot/untrusted-key defenses); real crypto sig verify + A/B transactional install + SLSA provenance blocked on crypto stack
  formal_verification:
    owner: src.verification (kernel_capabilities + os_enforcement)
    lane: A11
    maturity: partial
    note: sorry-free Lean proofs — single-use, container isolation, device-grant no-DMA-without-IOMMU, profile attenuation; VFS-transaction/WAL-ordering invariants pending
  evidence:
    owner: spipe sdn receipts
    lane: A11
    maturity: partial
    note: fail-closed on missing/stale artifacts not yet universal; first two consumers wired (duplicate_owner_spec ledger receipt + P6 lld_gate_receipt_spec blocked-artifact FAIL)
